<title>GERMANY: Kohl says expects tax reform deal in autumn.</title>
<headline>Kohl says expects tax reform deal in autumn.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Chancellor Helmut Kohl said on Friday that he expected agreement with Germany's upper house on a planned tax reform in the autumn.</p>
<p>&quot;I assume that we will reach an agreement in the upper house in the autumn,&quot; he told industrialists in Duesseldorf.</p>
<p>Talks aimed at resolving disagreements between Kohl's ruling coalition and the opposition Social Democrats, which control the upper house of parliament, collapsed this week, sending the dispute into a parliamentary battle.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 228 260 97150</p>
